      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your concern about your creative process being disrupted, but claims about specific consumer headphones emitting frequencies to suppress neurodivergent patterns are not scientifically substantiated. While sound frequencies can certainly affect mood and focus, there is no established evidence that standard wireless headphones operate in a manner to intentionally dampen cognitive functions. For potential improvements to your focus, you might consider low-frequency binaural beats or noise-canceling headphones designed to block external distractions.",
